{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And Moses said: Would that all HaShem's people were prophets, etc.</b> That is, perhaps they are true prophets, for the seventy that the Holy One, blessed be He, designated were from the spirit that was upon him, as it is written: ״ואצלתי מן הרוש אשר עליך״. But perhaps these are prophesying from the spirit of the Holy One, blessed be He. And in the first chapter of Sanhedrin it concludes: Granted, according to the one who says Moses is about to die, that is why it is written ״אדני משה כלאם״. But according to the one who says they were prophesying about the matter of levayah — for they were saying about him, levayah, levayah — and also according to the one who says they were prophesying about the matter of Gog and Magog, why כלאם? And it answers: it was not the way of the world that they should be like a student who rules a halakhah in the presence of his master, just as they wished to take the craft of Moses from him. And it further concludes: Granted, according to the one who says these two [Eldad and Medad] are what is meant by ״מי יתן את כל עם ה' נביאים״. But according to the one who says Moses is about to die — would that have been pleasing to him? And it answers: he did not complete it before them. What is כלאם? Impose upon them the needs of the public and they will expire on their own."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :register {:fixes 1}, :notes {0 "The Hebrew reads למאן דאמר על עסק שליו, which I render according to the Talmudic context (Sanhedrin 17a) where the elders are said to prophesy 'about the matter of levayah,' i.e., that Moses would die and the leadership would 'follow after' Joshua. The word שליו is rendered transliterated as levayah rather than translated, preserving the Talmudic idiom."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:18.404425293Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}